# SealedSecret TEMPLATE — turnstile-secrets (auth-experience signup CAPTCHA)
#
# ============================================================================
# THIS FILE IS A TEMPLATE. IT CONTAINS NO SECRET AND IS NOT APPLIED.
# ============================================================================
# The `.template` suffix keeps it out of the `fuzefront-sealed` Argo app
# (deploy/argocd/applications/fuzefront-sealed.yaml applies deploy/contabo/sealed/
# *.yaml only). Captcha is OFF by default: securityService.turnstile.siteKey is ""
# in every values overlay, so nothing references this Secret until the owner
# enables it. The security pod's secretKeyRef is `optional: true`, so even after
# the site key is set, a missing Secret/key leaves captcha OFF (fail-safe) — it
# never wedges the pod.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHY THIS IS NOT A PLACEHOLDER CIPHERTEXT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Turnstile SECRET KEY is issued by Cloudflare (dashboard > Turnstile > the
# FuzeFront widget) and is OWNER-GATED. It cannot be minted by
# `rotate-sealed-secret.yml` (that workflow generates random values; this one
# is externally issued). A fake `Ag...` blob would make the sealed-secrets
# controller report "illegal base64 data" and leave the `fuzefront-sealed` Argo
# app Degraded (this happened to unleash-secrets before it was properly sealed).
# So no encrypted-empty/placeholder SealedSecret is committed.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELEGATION (`@fuze` -> FuzeInfra) — when the owner has supplied the keys
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   Ask FuzeInfra (it owns the sealed-secrets controller + decrypt key) to seal,
#   against the cluster's published public cert, ONE value:
#
#     namespace : fuzefront
#     secret    : turnstile-secrets          (scope: strict, namespace+name bound)
#     key       : TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY       (the Cloudflare Turnstile secret key)
#     output    : this repo, deploy/contabo/sealed/turnstile-secrets.yaml
#                 (copy the block below, replace the placeholder with ciphertext)
#
#   Owner-side equivalent, no cluster access needed (cert is public):
#     deploy/scripts/seal-secret.sh TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY \
#       --scope fuzefront/turnstile-secrets \
#       --manifest deploy/contabo/sealed/turnstile-secrets.yaml
#   (hidden prompt / --in <file>; plaintext never touches git, chat or shell
#   history. Use a SEPARATE Secret rather than --merge-into fuzefront-secrets:
#   it keeps the large shared SealedSecret untouched and check-sealed-key-
#   regression.sh stays trivially green.)
#
#   The PUBLIC site key is NOT secret and is NOT sealed — it goes in values-prod.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GO-LIVE sequence (separate deploy-window changes; ORDER MATTERS)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   1. Land turnstile-secrets.yaml (ciphertext only); Argo `fuzefront-sealed`
#      applies it -> Secret/turnstile-secrets in ns fuzefront.
#   2. In values-prod.yaml set:
#        securityService.turnstile.siteKey:    "<public site key>"
#        securityService.turnstile.secretName: "turnstile-secrets"
#        (optional) securityService.turnstile.verifyTimeoutMs: "5000"
#      Argo rolls the security pod; AuthMethods.captcha is now advertised.
#   3. Only then flip the frontend flag fuzefront.auth.experience (repo variable
#      VITE_FF_AUTH_EXPERIENCE=true, release.yml) — together with or AFTER the
#      backend, never before: the UI must not render a widget the API does not
#      advertise.
#   Rotation: re-seal the key, merge, then restart the security pod (env from a
#   Secret is read at container start).
#
# Replace the entire block below with the sealing output.
---
apiVersion: bitnami.com/v1alpha1
kind: SealedSecret
metadata:
  name: turnstile-secrets
  namespace: fuzefront
spec:
  encryptedData:
    # Replace with sealed ciphertext. Do NOT commit plaintext.
    TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY: <REPLACE_WITH_KUBESEAL_OUTPUT>
  template:
    metadata:
      name: turnstile-secrets
      namespace: fuzefront
    type: Opaque
